Z||000004||My7Fieros||12-19-2001||09:48 PM||||I was actually gonna post a thread about this, but I cant my PIP to work! ARRRGG! Anyway Ive got two Fiero models...both are the 85 GT/86 SE style. Ive got one done up to look JUST like an Indy...I even put on the Indy decals that I bought off ebay! I then installed the 4 banger model engine in it I had from a 4 banger Fiero parts car model (no body) to make it just like an Indy. It mated right up to the stock V6 model tranny! And the other one I painted silver w/ grey int to match my daily driver. But on the silver one I did alittle "mini V8 Archie" and installed a V8 model engine out of a Trans Am model I bought. It took some modification, but it fit, looks stock, and it even mated up perfectly to the stock V6 model tranny! (I had to cut the tranny off the T/A engine...the block and tranny were one piece. Looks cool! Ive gotta get my PIP fixed!!!!!<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||Doni Hagan||12-19-2001||09:50 PM||||Hey...<P>The Monogram Fiero model that they SAY is an 85 GT is basically a notchback WITH rounded trim! It would make a perfect base for an 87 notchback model. I just traded mine to XDREWX for a fastback model but I know that other guys on the forum have'em. I wanna build a model of my car (87 GT) when it's completed.  <P>They're all over eBay. Don't let the "85" put you off. It ain't no 85!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>2Low...<BR>If you don't have a set yet, get some "Micro-Scale" polishing cloths to even out the body paint. If done right, it'll look like it's still wet when you're finished!!<p>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||1
