Z||000011||FIERO JOHN-WI||12-20-2001||08:41 AM||||Hey FieroKid87, I'm in the process of making a 88 formula (or you can call it that) read on and you will know what I mean further down in this post, and if you want to make a formula close to the real one or 87 coupe in your case you will need 2 kits, formula users you will need 3 kits:<BR>MAKING 87-88 YOU WILL NEED:<BR>85 Monogram Fiero GT kit<BR>85 MPC Black or Silver fiero on the box (NOT THE RED I REPEAT NOT THE RED 84 MPC  "HAS WRONG DECK LID"<BR>You use everything from the mpc kit, the only thing you use from the 85 Monogram kit for making 87-88 coupe is the rear battery covers and the wheels from it BUT remember the 2 modles are different scales!<P>MAKE 88 FORMULA YOU WILL NEED 4 KITS (IF YOU WANT TO MAKE IT AS LIFE LIKE AS POSSIBLE):<BR>85-MPC black or silver fiero on the box ONLY see above instructions for reason<BR>85 Monogram fiero GT<BR>MPC FIERO GT red or black one on the box doesn't matter<BR>89-90 Monogram firebird formula(red or black on the car box) <P>NOW HERES WHAT YOU WILL USE FROM EACH KIT TO MAKE A FORMULA:  <P>85 MPC kit you will use the complete body and interior (NOTE FOR THE FORMULA OR BASIC COUPE ABOVE YOU WILL HAVE TO SAND AND GRIND AND FILL IN THE FRONT AND REAR FASCIAS TO GET THEM TO LOOK LIKE THE 87-88 FASCIA AND IT WORKS (I HAVE DONE IT) I DON'T HAVE DIGITAL CAMERA TO SHOW YOU ALL, BUT WHEN I'M DONE (I'LL GET THEM OUT HERE)<BR>85 Monogram kit you will use the the battery covers, and the spoiler<BR>MPC Fiero GT you will use the V6 engine, and wheels and tires<BR>Lastly the Monogram Firebird formula(the only thing you use from the Monogram firebird is the formula decal Thats it!<P>Hopefully you have extra parts, so you don't have to open, unopen kits to make this (but if you got to have it "look real" then go ahead. (NOTE: I WILL TAKE ANYONES OLD AND BROKEN FIERO PIECES AFTER YOU BUILT YOU FIERO MODEL "ANYONE" JUST EMAIL ME)<P>I'm glad some one put this post on the forum hopefully more fiero guys will post pictures of thier model cars, as for my self I love fiero models(only) and I put a lot of detail into them,BUT I CAN'T PAINT A BODY TO SAVE MY LIFE, I have started 6 different fieros, but have not finished any of them (only work on them in the winter) the rest of the time I play with the real ones in the garage! ||||reg||1
Z||000012||rogergarrison||12-20-2001||09:22 AM||||a couple of my 1/8 scale (2' long) 'pretend' Fiero kitcars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1000860.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1000861.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Doni Hagan||12-20-2001||09:35 AM||||FIERO JOHN..<P>E-mail me next time you do a special model. My "kitbashing" skills are fair-to-midland but I'm getting to be a real SOB with an airbrush and polishing kit. I can give you some good hints on painting and even spray one for you if you want.<P>In order for me to build an accurate replica of my car, I'm gonna need to "bash" the ERTL/AMT Fiero GT, a 2001-2 Mustang GT, a Ferrari 306 or GTO, Monogram's Acura model (beautiful wheels / alone worth the price of the kit) and some serious aftermarket photoetched detail stuff. I probably won't have this thing finished until spring.   <P>||||reg||1
